      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XVIII.—For the second line compare Panchatantra (Bomb.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "Sans. Classics) I. p. 2 and Bhâminîvilâsa I., 12. The idea is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "very common in our poetry.—Vasantatilakâ.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XIX.—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XX.—नाम is an idiomatic equivalent to “indeed,” and is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "in very common use. Compare Bhavabhûti's well known words",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "ये नाम केचिदिह नः &c., or the equally well-known न नाम शरासनम् of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "the Vikramorvashî, and various other places प्रच्छन्नगुप्तम्=प्रच्छन्नं यथा",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "स्यात्तथा गुप्तम्. Râmarshi has प्रच्छन्नं च तद्गुप्तं च. It means carefully pro-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "tected. On गुरूणां गुरुः, the commentator has the following क्षुद्रगुरवः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "सर्वविद्यासंपूर्णप्राज्ञं प्रष्टुमायान्ति स प्राज्ञो गुरूणामपि गुरुः ॥ अथ च गृणाति हितमुपदिशति",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "इति गुरुरिति गुरुपदव्याख्यानमतो हितकर्त्री विद्यैव. This is too far-fetched,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "and not free from difficulties. गुरूणां गुरुः is simply greatest of the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "great. गुरु is feminine (Pâṇini IV., 1, 44). For the genitive see",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "Pâṇini II., 3, 41. राजसु is understood by the commentator as a Lo-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "cative, which is probably right. But it is somewhat difficult to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "account for it, having regard to Pâṇini II., 3, 67. To suit this",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "rule राजसुपूजिता might be taken as a compound सु going with",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "पूजिता.—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXI.—The commentator says देहिनां प्राणिनां यदि क्षान्तिः क्षमा",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "वर्तते तदा सान्त्वनवचनेन किं प्रयोजनम् तथा च क्रोधोस्ति तर्हि अरिभिः शत्रुभिः किम् ॥",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "ज्ञातिश्चेदनलेन किम् । दायादाः सहजारय इति वर्तते ॥ ज्ञातयो यदा निन्दादिपरुषं",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "वदन्ति तेनैव दाहो भवति अग्नेः किं प्रयोजनम् ॥ .... यदि व्रीडा लज्जा असत्कर्मसु",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "वर्तते तदा तदेव भूषणमितरभूषणैः किम् ॥ Compare Stanza 55 below.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "The meaning of the questions is—What more of good or evil (as",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "the case may be) can accrue from the one than from the other?",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "This Stanza also occurs at Kâvyasangraha p. 2.—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXII.—कला is art, in both senses of the word. “On them",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "rests the world.” i. e. Without these qualities, society would",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "be in disorder. Râmarshi renders लोके स्थितिः by जीवनमर्यादा.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
